# The scenario-catalog validator, for the Scenario Catalog CI job and for
# running `pwpf-validate-catalog` by hand. Regenerate the pinned lock with:
#   pip-compile -c requirements.txt --output-file=requirements-ai.txt --strip-extras requirements-ai.in
#
# The `-c requirements.txt` is load-bearing. This lock now resolves the
# framework and therefore its whole dependency set, and compiled on its own it
# picked newer versions of playwright, allure-pytest and pytest-rerunfailures
# than the test-runtime lock - two locks disagreeing about the framework's
# dependencies, for no reason. Constraining it to the test-runtime lock keeps
# the two in step, so regenerate requirements.txt first.
#
# The validator is framework code (pwpf/ai_testing/validate_catalog.py) that
# operates on this project's data: it reads this repository's pytest.ini,
# apps/*/scenarios/ and tests/ from the resolved project root. So the
# dependency is the framework with its `ai` extra, which carries the PyYAML and
# jsonschema the validator needs, at the same pinned tag requirements.in uses.
#
# Kept separate from requirements.txt for the reason it always was: the catalog
# job runs no pytest and no browser, so it installs this file alone.
playwright-pytest-framework[ai] @ git+https://github.com/abhay-scaler/playwright-pytest-framework@v0.1.0
